From 899e42a4850a72693316e09b7de874cd8f0e08d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatyana <7694826+ta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:39:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [add] desktop reorder, close and activation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- MoveDesktop() takes a target position, so a desktop can be inserted at
  a given index instead of always at the end; within one monitor this is
  a pure reorder and the active desktop is tracked by set reference, so
  the wrong windows are never hidden afterwards
- CloseDesktop() removes a desktop and hands its windows to the
  neighbour (previous, or the next one when closing the first) — upstream
  had no way to remove a desktop at all
- ActivateWindow() switches to the desktop owning a window, restores it
  if minimised and raises it
- windows moved by hand are restored when their desktop becomes active,
  so a window dropped onto a desktop arrives open, not minimised
- overview window lists are sorted by title; the backing set has no
  order, so they were reshuffled on every refresh
